From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msado15: Recordset.Open reads a recordset that Save wrote (MSPersist), from a file or a Stream.

Recordset.Save wrote ADO's XML format, but nothing could read it back: a file name without a connection was "Unsupported Active connection type", Provider=MSPersist an unknown provider, a Stream an invalid argument. As ADO does, Open of a file (adCmdFile, Provider=MSPersist, or a file name with no connection) or of a Stream reads the schema (field names, rs:name, types from dt:type and rs:dbtype, sizes, precision and scale, rs:long, rs:fixedlength, nullability) and the rows through MSXML; an absent attribute is Null. The changes pending when it was saved come back pending: rs:insert rows are new, rs:update pairs are changed rows with their rs:original values (Field.OriginalValue reads them, as it now does for any row changed in a batch), rs:delete rows are deleted, for UpdateBatch. The recordset is disconnected, static, client-cursor, batch optimistic. Save writes the types the way ADO does so they come back: currency with rs:dbtype='currency', numeric/decimal as number, timestamps, ANSI text with rs:dbtype='str', long values with rs:long. Save now works on a copy of its VARIANT argument: on x86_64 that is the caller's memory, cleared by IDispatch::Invoke afterwards, and a Stream saved to was released once too often.
---
--- a/dlls/msado15/recordset.c
+++ b/dlls/msado15/recordset.c
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
